# Atlas prepare

Import HostFiles from "./host_files.lg".
Import HostTools from "./host_tools.lg".

A release made into the chunk files the streamed ingest reads: a `.gz` copied
(the source is never touched) and decompressed with `gzip`, then cut with
`split -C` into pieces of at most `chunkMb` megabytes that end at line ends — the
atlas is pretty-printed, so a piece never cuts a character in two.

## To runStep (program: Text, arguments: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    Inspect runTool(program, arguments, 600000, 65536):
        When Err (e):
            Return program + ": " + e.
        When Ok (r):
            If r's exitCode is not equal to 0:
                Return program + " failed: " + r's stderr.
            Return "".
    Return program + ": unrun".

## Note
The chunk paths of a release, in order.

## To prepareAtlas (path: Text, workDir: Text, chunkMb: Int) -> Result of Seq of Text and Text:
    Let made be ensureDir(workDir + "/parts").
    Let mutable plain be path.
    If endsWith(path, ".gz"):
        Let copied be runStep("cp", [path, workDir + "/atlas.json.gz"]).
        Let unzipped be runStep("gzip", ["-d", "-f", workDir + "/atlas.json.gz"]).
        If copied + unzipped is not equal to "":
            Return a new Err with error copied + unzipped.
        Set plain to workDir + "/atlas.json".
    Let cut be runStep("split", ["-C", "{chunkMb}M", "-d", "-a", "5", plain, workDir + "/parts/atlas."]).
    If cut is not equal to "":
        Return a new Err with error cut.
    Inspect listNames(workDir + "/parts"):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (names):
            Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
            Repeat for name in names:
                Push workDir + "/parts/" + name to out.
            Return a new Ok with value out.
    Return a new Err with error "unprepared".
